>>
Rule 1 (argument must be a non-empty sequence of tensors)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor) ⊎ list(tensor)} |= v_1.len ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (at least one index array must be provided)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len ≥ 1
>>
Rule 3 (single index must be 1-D and of integer or boolean dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4)
>>
Rule 4 (two indices must each be 1-D and of integer or boolean dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1) ∧ ((dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4))
>>
Rule 5 (three indices must each be 1-D and of integer or boolean dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_3) = 1) ∧ ((dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4) ∧ (dtype_(v_3) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 4))
>>
Rule 6 (index arrays cannot be floating-point, complex, or string typed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 7 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 8 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 7 (1-D index arrays may be empty but must have non-negative length)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 0
